      "pattern": "const run = useCallback(",
      "description": "Everything starts here. The ✦ Ask Claude button, Ctrl+Enter and the question popover all call `run(scope, question)`. It keeps a `pending` counter so the UI can show a spinner, and hands the Excalidraw API object plus the chosen scope to `askClaude` in src/claude.js. That function holds the client-side half of the core logic. The rest of App.jsx is the board shell (autosave, pens), which this tour skips.",
