    {
      "file": "src/claude.js",
      "line": 104,
      "endLine": 127,
      "pattern": "function selectTargets(api, scope) {",
      "description": "`selectTargets` turns a scope into two element sets. **context** goes into the overview image. **focus** is what Claude should actually respond to. In *auto* mode a selection wins. Otherwise the focus is the \"new ink\": elements updated more than 500 ms after the newest answer card's `askedAt`. For either case it adds a 700px margin of surrounding content. *Visible page* and *Whole board* use the viewport or everything, and keep a focus only when it is a strict subset.",
      "vaayu": {
        "title": "What does Claude look at?",
        "takeaway": "Focus = what to answer; context = what to read around it.",
        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "sel",
            "line": 111,
            "pattern": "if ((scope === \"auto\" || scope === \"selection\") && selected.length) {",
            "label": "Selection takes priority"
          },
          {
            "id": "fresh",
            "line": 116,
            "pattern": "if (scope === \"auto\" && fresh.length) {",
            "label": "Otherwise: ink since last answer"
          },
          {
            "id": "newink",
            "line": 93,
            "pattern": "function newInk(all) {",
            "label": "Compares updated vs last askedAt"
          }
        ],
        "connections": [
          {
            "from": "fresh",
            "to": "newink",
            "label": "fresh = newInk(all)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "src/claude.js",
      "line": 67,
      "endLine": 89,
      "pattern": "function expand(picked, all) {",
      "description": "`expand` keeps the snapshots coherent. Picking elements by bounding box can split a shape from its label, or one group member from the rest. This fixed-point loop keeps pulling in bound text, containers, group siblings and frame children until nothing changes. `selectTargets` calls it on every set it returns, so Claude never sees a box without its text."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/claude.js",
      "line": 130,
      "endLine": 177,
      "pattern": "function summarize(elements, focusIds) {",
      "description": "Images alone can blur typed text and miss arrow wiring, so `summarize` adds a compact text outline: free text, shapes with their labels, and arrows written as `from \"A\" to \"B\"` using their bindings. Focus elements get a `[NEW]` tag. Freehand strokes are only counted, because handwriting has to be read from the image. Claude's own cards are skipped here. `priorAnswers` (just below) sends them separately in full, nearest and most recent first, so Claude can continue the conversation without repeating itself.",
      "vaayu": {
        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "arrow",
            "line": 161,
            "pattern": "if (from || to || lbl) lines.push(",
            "label": "Arrow connections as text"
          },
          {
            "id": "strokes",
            "line": 174,
            "pattern": "if (strokes) lines.push(",
            "label": "Handwriting deferred to the image"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "src/claude.js",
      "line": 230,
      "endLine": 259,
      "pattern": "export function findFreeSpot(w, h, anchor, obstacles) {",
      "description": "The README promises that Claude never draws over your content, and this function is how. It builds candidate positions around the anchor (right, below, left, above), sliding outward in 40px steps. Each candidate gets a distance cost plus a directional penalty, and the cheapest spot whose padded rectangle clears every obstacle wins. If nothing fits, it falls back to the right of everything. It is called twice: once for the placeholder, and again for the final card once its real size is known.",
      "vaayu": {
        "title": "Never draw over the user",
        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "free",
            "line": 233,
            "pattern": "const free = (x, y) =>",
            "label": "Rectangle overlap test"
          },
          {
            "id": "cost",
            "line": 253,
            "pattern": "const cost = Math.hypot(x - bx, y - ay) + pen;",
            "label": "Distance + direction penalty"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "server/api.js",
      "line": 156,
      "endLine": 199,
      "pattern": "async function handleAsk(req, res) {",
      "description": "Now on the server. `handleAsk` gives each request a timestamped id, writes `board.png` (and `focus.png` if there is a focus) into `data/asks/<id>/`, builds the prompt and saves it as `prompt.txt` for debugging. If the browser disconnects, it kills the Claude child process so abandoned asks don't keep running. The response returns the parsed answer along with duration, cost and session id.",
      "vaayu": {
        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "write",
            "line": 166,
            "pattern": "await fsp.writeFile(contextPath, Buffer.from(png(image), \"base64\"));",
            "label": "Snapshot saved to disk"
          },
          {
            "id": "prompt",
            "line": 172,
            "pattern": "const prompt = buildPrompt({",
            "label": "Build prompt with file paths"
